    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence number, and moved every value derived from it onto the new identity.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (model \u2014 the single source of truth for derived values):\n- Added a shared private `sha256Hex(String)` helper (full lower-case hex digest) and refactored `householdId` to use it.\n- Added `customerCode(postcode, telephone, lastName)`: `REGION` comes from `regionForPostcode` (falling back to `UNKNOWN` when the postcode is absent/out of range), and `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n- Replaced the old `locality(postcode, city)` with `locality(customerCode)`, which takes the `REGION` segment (text before the first `-`), returning `UNKNOWN` when there's no code \u2014 so locality now rides the region-and-hash identity.\n- `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` are unchanged in logic; they automatically reflect the new code since they're built from it.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.java`**: `generateCustomerCode` now delegates to `Owner.customerCode(...)` (no repository/sequence lookup, removed the unused `codePrefix`). The create audit record logs `owner.getCustomerCode()` unchanged, so it now emits the new identity (verified in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**: `formatLocality` now calls `Owner.locality(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to match.\n\nThe `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` column comfortably holds the new format (max `UNKNOWN-XXXXXXXX` = 16 chars). The acceptance test asserting `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` passes.\n\nOne behavioural note worth flagging: because `REGION` is now postcode-only, an owner created **without** a postcode gets `UNKNOWN-\u2026` and therefore locality `UNKNOWN`, even for a known city like Sydney \u2014 the city-fallback that the old `locality` had is intentionally gone per the spec (\"the region code derived from the postcode\"). The city\u2192region table is retained solely for postcode validation.",
